From a5493d83901a6ce6d86ecf4c6a1a9eff12b49adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:05:16 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/4] KVM: s390: Run ESA/390 DAT-on code on shadow address
 spaces

The ESA/390-compatibility mode has no dynamic address translation. While
the PSW of a vCPU in the mode has the DAT bit, run the vCPU with DAT off on
an ESA/390 shadow gmap instead of the VM's gmap. The PSW given to SIE lacks
the DAT bit and the interruption masks, so the machine presents no
interruption itself; KVM presents them, and kicks the vCPU out of SIE when
one becomes pending. SIGP orders are not interpreted by the machine for
such a VM, so that their interruptions take the same path.

Intercept what would show the substitution or apply real addresses to
the shadow: program interruptions, SVC, LPSW, SSM, STOSM, STNSM, LCTL of
control registers 0, 1, 6 and 14, the storage-key instructions and
TPROT. Emulate LOAD REAL ADDRESS and the purges (IPTE, CSP, PTLB, PALB)
also with DAT off. LPSW accepts a wait PSW with an odd instruction
address, which is recognized only when an instruction is fetched. IPTE
and the purge of CSP take effect on all vCPUs before the instruction
completes: the shadow entries are removed, and vCPUs running on a
dropped shadow are kicked out of SIE first.

The primary and the home space are provided. SET ADDRESS SPACE CONTROL
(FAST) and INSERT ADDRESS SPACE CONTROL arrive as special-operation
exceptions and are emulated, including the space-switch event.

SIE needs the prefix page of the address space it runs on, which in the
shadow is virtual page 0. While the guest's tables do not translate that
page, a page of the vCPU stands in for it. Stores to its first 512 bytes
are caught with low-address protection given to SIE and presented as the
translation exception the guest's tables call for; other stores, as the
change bit shows them, fail KVM_RUN.

KVM_RUN also fails with -EOPNOTSUPP while the PSW has the DAT bit and the
secondary space or access-register mode is selected, or branch or ASN
tracing is enabled. Explicit tracing is taken out of control register 12
for SIE: TRACE records nothing while translated.

Nothing enables this yet.
